schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: Gitcoin GG24 round (Oct-Nov 2025) distributed over $1.8 million
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    "Gitcoin's GG24 round in October, November 2025 distributed over $1.8
    million across themed domains using its 3.0 model." Also noted: Gitcoin's
    older Grants Stack platform wound down in May 2025, and rounds now run
    across multiple platforms (including Giveth), not one central app.
    Separately, "one Local Node round [ReFi DAO via Gitcoin/Giveth match
    pools] offered a $25k matching pool on Celo."
  evidence: >-
    Stated in the article's "External Funding" section; the article's
    References list Gitcoin Grants (grants.gitcoin.co) and Giveth
    (giveth.io) generally but does not link a specific GG24 results page or
    the $25k Celo round announcement.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/funding-your-node.md (no specific results-page URL cited)
  interpretation: >-
    Plausible given Gitcoin's known scale and public shift away from a single
    Grants Stack app toward a multi-platform model; consistent with figures
    reported elsewhere in the site's Giveth-focused article for a different,
    Ethereum Security-themed round.
  uncertainty: >-
    Both dollar figures ($1.8M for GG24; $25k Celo matching pool) are
    unsourced to a specific, checkable URL in this article and are
    time-bound program history that will go stale; verify against Gitcoin's
    and ReFi DAO's live pages before repeating as current.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/funding-your-node.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
